  "body": "**Stacked on #522** (the Haas, Mazak and Siemens probing hooks). Review only this PR's own commit, `8f0a6d1b`.\n\nThe Haas part of #392. #465 made the Fanuc post probe on an inverted X/Y behind the manifest flag `probeAxisInversion`, and left Haas until its probing hooks landed.\n\n## What changed\n- **`haas.cps` declares `probeAxisInversion = true`.** #522's Haas hooks write the same controller words as Fanuc:\n  - G31, the trip read from `#5061-#5063`, and a `#3000=2` no-contact alarm;\n  - a `G91 G1` back-off and the deviation into `#190..`;\n  - `G10 L2 P.. X[#5221+#190]`.\n  - Each reads in the controller's own frame, so #465's mirrored stream gives the **physical** correction with no Haas-specific code. A comment in the probing section says why.\n  - The `onProbeGuard` positioning moves mirror correctly too.\n- **`invert.rs`:** the refusal text now names \"Fanuc and Haas\". `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` is updated to match.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/392-haas-probe-inverted.md`. It records the reasoning, what was dropped (a separate Haas macro reader; relying on G101 or the control's axis-direction setting) and the sources.\n\n## How tested\n- **`inverted_probe` (9) now runs every case for both posts:**\n  - the cases: face −Z / −X, edge −Y, corners +X+Y / −X−Y, bore and boss;\n  - each on standard, inverted X, inverted Y and inverted XY machines;\n  - G55 lands on the physical datum, and a part where the model says leaves the datum unchanged;\n  - no contact alarms `#3000=2`, and out of tolerance alarms `#3000=1`;\n  - the converse also holds: the untranslated program misses, and undoing any one translated word breaks it.\n- **New tests:**\n  - `an_uninverted_program_is_unchanged_by_the_flag`: both posts give byte-identical standard-machine output, and #173's Haas golden is unchanged;\n  - `probing_through_an_unverified_script_still_refuses_by_name`: the refusal is pinned on a shipped script with its flag stripped.\n- **Gate:** inverted_post 15, probe_dialects 13, conformance, golden_cl, posting, fanuc_post, inverted_equivalence, probe_op, axis_direction and camcraft-post pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n**Sources:** the Haas Mill Operator's Manual (public), as #522 cites: G31, `#5061-#5063`, `#5221+`, `#3000`/`#3006`, `G10 L2`. The inversion adds no new controller semantics.\n\n**Not exercised:** a real Haas control with an inverted axis.\n\nChangelog: Probing posts on a Haas machine with an inverted X/Y axis (the probe records are mirrored like moves; the written work offset is the physical correction) (#392)\n\nFixes #392\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
